# https://github.com/browserslist/browserslist#readme
#
# Dynamic Framework 3.x targets.
#
# The 3.x architecture depends on two CSS features the 2.x list excluded:
#
#   @layer       Chrome 99, Safari 15.4, Firefox 97    (2022)
#   color-mix()  Chrome 111, Safari 16.2, Firefox 113  (2023)
#
# Neither is decoration. @layer is what lets a client's own (unlayered) CSS win
# over the framework without !important — which is what removes _shame.scss and
# the $enable-important-utilities flag. color-mix() is what replaces the
# --bs-*-rgb channel, which doubled the 2.x colour system and could not be
# expressed as a Figma variable.
#
# The floors below are the exact versions those two features require, rounded
# up to a release boundary — NOT the `baseline widely available` query, which
# resolves to Safari 17.4 / Chrome 123 and so drops users this system can
# actually serve.
#
# Raising the floor is a 3.0 breaking change, made once and deliberately: 2.x
# listed Chrome 60 (2017), Safari 12 (2018) and `op_mini all`, none of which can
# render a token-driven system at all.

Chrome >= 111
Edge >= 111
Firefox >= 113
Safari >= 16.4
iOS >= 16.4
Samsung >= 22
Opera >= 97
not dead
